{"title":"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Case_1:_is_odd\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 1:  is odd</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Case_1:_is_even\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 1:  is even</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43ec2086760ce93aaca1938b12c93cbf7cf9dc76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> be a sequence determined by the rule <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1c2e08f6bbbcf7c5cc64f53365cdbb19c9e1b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=a_{n-1}/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896d56965b17443a55b2b5e55f798adf6465380d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8df54e3b84063c1be0bfae4f7daf50d48a235c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=3a_{n-1}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896d56965b17443a55b2b5e55f798adf6465380d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03a47d044f9e0bd9666519d7c79affb9f00f5fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 \\le 2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> is it true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is less than each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e28850813a5321d2a8ae3c0510457a7337975ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555010b284aa17f892666e5567d3e6cc872d17b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 250\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 251\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 501\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 502\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)} 1004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"436\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All positive integers can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b417a127620d5b467fe7a48ad5f7d843e5c390b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd562ceaa0577b4a7f23a01f24b17de924542bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/2623d8aec5bfc8565c8d35b6694000c972e9fc8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5dac6132726ffa3d36b5e91034f7e39fa0af3f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a nonnegative integer. \n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/297d1e4970c1fad5999b43fda2dea3d8a0e977a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/1/dc148750d521df05deff635604689b7e981faf08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=\\frac{4n}{2}=2n&lt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa8ae90f591ece3f22d17fe2e15ff1bdaff7c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=4n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10df694e869dd0e69f425c71ce29449f3cda9d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=3(4n+1)+1=12n+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"234\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6e0527af4e52edda1beea002a993be4ff2e04d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=\\frac{12n+4}{2}=6n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"180\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d82293a7b38d042c36a6439c6e92d74f788a043.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=\\frac{6n+2}{2}=3n+1&lt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"211\" height=\"37\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00be6351f2bd7c53ecdbd2d3b5cb9137b76df63d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=4n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a5e892beab68523959e3a7b584692c4ba48a2c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=2n+1&lt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca75bdabb1a7191ad6cbfa12d8b81aab1e8338ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2b54962bdbc45536994912e6c5592cc0916b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=3(4n+3)+1=12n+10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c12bb84ed140cef6e33fad1691670604ceee71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=\\frac{12n+10}{2}=6n+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"190\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1af4535dcc6f42c23cf4938f180b0c7998cf356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=3(6n+5)+1=18n+16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"18\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d2beb6dbb0390a90d44cfa206cfd23a318c24e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12n+10, 6n+5, 18n+16 &gt; 4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"281\" height=\"16\" />, every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca75bdabb1a7191ad6cbfa12d8b81aab1e8338ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> will satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aade51fb35432020d17abc780f2d4acaaa884656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1&lt;a_2,a_3,a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Since one fourth of the positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03a47d044f9e0bd9666519d7c79affb9f00f5fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 \\le 2008$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5dac6132726ffa3d36b5e91034f7e39fa0af3f9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a nonnegative integer, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56a2933cf3bff6723564b2494feaf1d92e40e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2008 = 502 \\Rightarrow D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After checking the first few <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can see that the only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> that satisfy the conditions are odd numbers that when tripled and added 1 to, are double an odd number. For example, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78dc60f470ddfefd5bc127b3db63b6c7013b778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, we notice the sequence yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, a valid sequence.\n</p><p>So we can set up an equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ad6ca913b22d14e662ee1d6af8a5daab244fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 1 = 2(2k - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> where x is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. Rearranging the equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/1233b3f1617155e41730ac341a5897a4a108edb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3x + 3)/4 = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />. Experimenting yields that every 4th <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> after 3 creates an integer, and thus satisfies the sequence condition. So the number of valid solutions is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/909b80466ee1a71cdf47c7935d8719bc64a8cfc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2008/4 = 502 \\Rightarrow D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can easily see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be even since for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7cd5c94359c469e123d705d4abdf693aa26a1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;\\dfrac{x}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> must be odd, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b1834a0bc7cdc886423d4bcffb3b19ab7a0f9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=3a_1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> must be even, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63721289f9399fcf067489c6fd946a85bc58c542.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=\\dfrac{a_2}2=\\dfrac{3a_1+1}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" />. Now, let's see if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> are greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b1834a0bc7cdc886423d4bcffb3b19ab7a0f9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=3a_1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />, and we can easily see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd69c69516a6681e8913f7287fa4f364e3c942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+1&gt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so for all odd positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef15b6e5291f1febed83efa560ad246b453d6216.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. Now, let's see if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b2f54508f6c72b8bd4f26022ea78ad1b4dff32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b2f54508f6c72b8bd4f26022ea78ad1b4dff32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c3d0ff8663274e3e7c516946ff7ebf95bab6e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3a_1+1}2&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f895ef3fb1b055803e3c9f6c90cc4e92a76c8948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a_1+1&gt;2a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16aef860961c65e662185bcd6784609cc26c7f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1&gt;-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" />, and that is true for all odd positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, so we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b2f54508f6c72b8bd4f26022ea78ad1b4dff32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> for all odd positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. Now, we have two cases!\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_1:_is_odd\">Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69cddacc22fafdf2875660cd67e847eecc4d54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{a_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is odd</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Case 1:  is odd\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>\\noindent That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd3e0040cee5c64f4157eb1fc1d8590d7c89455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=3a_3+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b11a1127a3a72b703f1839245beb3770aa5dfbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4&gt;a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> must be true. Since we also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b2f54508f6c72b8bd4f26022ea78ad1b4dff32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> is true, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b255f47fb728ee64afe055f595eb49a21dbcc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, this case always works! Now, let's see when would <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> be odd. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is odd, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> should contain exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> two. That means we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/7811987b121af2e004ad402100a92474dc98a0e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,6,10,14,18,22,26,\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"17\" />. For there to exist an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> must be one more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563605a824d279ef0181b5a8a80a44cf611147c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=10,22,34,46,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"17\" /> which corresponds to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54bfa2ff3b7cb6cf83ea22609e59ef8584ab718c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=3,7,11,15,\\ldots,2007$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"17\" />, so this case gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f563574744d6a2d6761415d8edfe3b33182be38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$502$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_1:_is_even\">Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/9/d69cddacc22fafdf2875660cd67e847eecc4d54c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{a_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is even</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Case 1:  is even\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>\\noindent That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e50f2d9edbce7302d2062a4e0e40ad6b4ed8e1ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=\\dfrac{a_3}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"34\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b07b368bb1887b3ec3cf162841116dcb40f3258.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_4=\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{3a_1+1}2\\right)}2=\\dfrac{3a_1+1}4.\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"62\" />If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28b255f47fb728ee64afe055f595eb49a21dbcc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/0417645d90a7a1233af9bc60088a14128424b2b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3a_1+1}4&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917d5cf7be3c8637b44201c32f3d387323a55baa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a_1+1&gt;4a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b41f91930b1ee2ddbc59e4a9e2bebaf90e07325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />. But, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> must be a positive integer, there cannot exist any possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b41f91930b1ee2ddbc59e4a9e2bebaf90e07325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&gt;a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, so this case will not give any possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />.\n\\noindent\\textbf{Conclusion}\n</p><p>\\noindent Totaling up our two cases, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265939f49e91bdbd54de6f0c45e2f5493e9ed9d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$502+0=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 502}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"157\" height=\"32\" /> possible positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> exist.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A\">2008 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <